  "question": {
    "text": "In a historical experiment to determine Planck&#39;s constant, a metal surface was irradiated with light of different wavelengths. The emitted photoelectron energies were measured by applying a stopping potential. The relevant data for the wavelength <math><mo>(</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>)</mo></math> of incident light and the corresponding stopping potential <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfenced></math> are given below:<br />&nbsp;<table border=\"1\" style=\"width: 100px; height: 100px;\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td><math><mi>&#955;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>V</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>0.3</td>\t\t\t<td>2.0</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>0.4</td>\t\t\t<td>1.0</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>0.5</td>\t\t\t<td>0.4</td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table><br />Given that <math><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>m</mi><msup><mrow><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>19</mn></mrow></msup><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi></math> Planck&#39;s constant (in units of J s) found from such an experiment is :",
